<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Trust Territory of Somaliland</h1><p class="st-meta">1950 CE – 1960 CE · capital Mogadishu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The UN trust territory administered by Italy for ten years to prepare southern Somalia for independence in 1960.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After British military administration from 1941, the UN decided in 1949 that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> would return to its former colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a> as administering power, on condition that the territory become independent after ten years. The Italian Trusteeship Administration, AFIS, took over in April 1950, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was supervised by a UN advisory council and built up schools, a civil service and elected councils. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-youth-league">Somali Youth League</a>, the leading nationalist party, won the elections of 1956 and 1959, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a> took over ministries under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullahi-issa">Abdullahi Issa</a>. Bananas remained the main export, and Somali was not yet a written official language.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 1 July 1960 the territory became independent and united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-somaliland">State of Somaliland</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-republic">Somali Republic</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden-abdullah-osman">Aden Abdullah Osman</a> as president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/trust-territory-of-somaliland.jpg" alt="Trust Territory of Somaliland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Republica Italiana · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1946%E2%80%932003).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1950 CE – 1960 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mogadishu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullahi Issa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, Italian, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Amministrazione fiduciaria italiana della Somalia, AFIS</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1955&amp;focus=trust-territory-of-somaliland" aria-label="Trust Territory of Somaliland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5939 2101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Trust Territory of Somaliland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6259 2357L6259 2357M6259 2357L5304 942M6259 2357L6259 2357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6259 2357h0M5304 942h0M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6259 2357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mogadishu. <a href="/atlas?year=1955&amp;focus=trust-territory-of-somaliland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
